            <ArticleTitle>Dexmedetomidine as a Supplement to Spinal Anesthesia Block: A Case Report of Three Infants.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-128</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1213/XAA.0000000000000545</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a novel use for dexmedetomidine as a supplemental intravenous or intranasal sedative for spinal anesthesia in infants. The children were 1, 2, and 9 months old having either inguinal hernia repair or circumcision. None of them experienced clinically relevant hemodynamic changes or apnea. Pain scores were zero throughout the postoperative period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
